highs of any decade (51). Buffalo's all-time high is 99\u00b0F, on August 27, 1948.","t_chg":"Buffalo's days and nights both warmed. Days warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 152 complete years: Buffalo's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.09\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.03 to +0.15), about +1.4\u00b0F since 1874. Buffalo's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.31\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.26 to +0.36), about +4.7\u00b0F since 1874.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 4 of 12 months. Highs rose in 10 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Buffalo has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Buffalo's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.39 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.18 to +0.60), about +6.1 inches since 1871. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 40.6 inches a year. The wettest year was 1878 (60.24 in); the driest, 1941 (22.16 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 1 daily record high, no daily record lows"}}